        "description": "Job Summary:\nWe are seeking a proactive and data-driven Amazon Executive to take ownership of our daily operations for physical products on Amazon Seller Central. Your primary responsibilities will revolve around end-to-end marketplace management, including seller account handling, listing optimization, FBA fulfillment flow, Amazon PPC (with a focus on Sponsored Display), and inventory stocking.\nNote: While daily operations are the core of this role, candidates with proven experience in Product Development and Launching will be highly prioritized during the selection process.\nKey Responsibilities:\n1. Seller Account Handling & Customer Service\n• Manage daily operations on Amazon Seller Central.\n• Actively monitor and maintain Account Health metrics (ODR, LSR, VTR) to ensure 100% policy compliance and prevent listing suppression or account suspension risks.\n• Handle customer inquiries, monitor product reviews/Q&A, and manage case logs to resolve disputes, FBA discrepancies, or A-to-Z claims efficiently.\n2. Listing Creation & SEO Optimization\n• Create and manage highly optimized product listings (SEO, keyword indexing) aligned with the Amazon A9 algorithm.\n• Craft compelling Titles, Bullet Points, Product Descriptions, and Backend Search Terms to maximize organic visibility and conversion rates (CVR).\n• Coordinate with the creative team to develop high-converting visual assets, A+ Content (Enhanced Brand Content), and manage the Amazon Brand Storefront.\n3. FBA Fulfillment Flow (Order, Shipping, Delivery)\n• Manage the end-to-end FBA (Fulfillment by Amazon) logistics flow for physical products.\n• Create FBA inbound shipment plans, generate Amazon barcodes/labels (FNSKU), and ensure compliance with Amazon's receiving guidelines.\n• Coordinate seamlessly with 3PL partners, freight forwarders, and internal supply chain teams to track shipments from factory to Amazon Fulfillment Centers (or AWD warehouses).\n4. Amazon Advertising (PPC) & Sponsored Display\n• Set up, manage, and optimize Amazon PPC campaigns, utilizing Sponsored Display to retarget audiences, cross-sell, and increase brand awareness.\n• Monitor daily ad performance, implement bid optimizations, and harvest search terms to achieve target ACOS (Advertising Cost of Sales), TACOS (Total ACOS), and ROAS (Return on Ad Spend).\n5. Inventory & Stocking\n• Develop robust sales forecasts and demand planning models using historical data and seasonality trends.\n• Monitor daily inventory levels to ensure a healthy Inventory Performance Index (IPI).\n• Create replenishment plans to prevent OOS (Out of Stock) situations while avoiding overstocking and long-term storage fees.\n6. Product Development & Launching (Highly Prioritized for Selection)\n• Market Research: Utilize tools like Helium 10, Keepa, or Jungle Scout to validate market demand, analyze competitors, and identify high-potential product opportunities.\n• Launching Strategy: Build and execute end-to-end product launch roadmaps. Leverage Amazon programs (e.g., Vine) and promotional strategies to drive initial traction, BSR (Best Sellers Rank), and reviews during the critical \"honeymoon period\".\n• Product Enhancement: Collaborate with R&D and Sourcing teams to define product specifications and optimize the Bill of Materials (BOM) based on customer insights.",
